//! The documents a client has open, laid over the files on disk.
//!
//! Each open document belongs to the package whose manifest is nearest above it. A package is
//! opened as `silk check` opens it, on one revisable semantic store. An edit only replaces a
//! document's text and marks its package stale; [`refresh`] then publishes every open document of
//! a stale package over the package's disk revision and updates the store once, so a burst of
//! edits costs one update.
//!
//! Syntax diagnostics come from parsing each changed document alone, so refreshing for them runs no
//! semantic unit. Semantic diagnostics come from a work queue: each [`work`] step checks one module
//! of a package with `Semantic.checkModule`, the modules of open documents first and then the rest
//! of the package, so the server can answer requests between steps. A module whose kept sweep no
//! longer verifies is first prepared one declaration per step with `Semantic.prepareDeclaration`,
//! so a request waits at most for one declaration rather than for a whole module. A module's
//! diagnostics are the rejections located in it, whichever module's check reached them.

